OpenHSP for Debian/Ubuntu
=========================

The command-line hspcmp entry point is a wrapper around
/usr/lib/openhsp/hspcmp. It supplies the packaged common include directory and
runtime directory by default:

  --compath=/usr/lib/openhsp/common/
  --syspath=/usr/lib/openhsp/

Pass a later --compath or --syspath option if a project needs a custom tree.

GPIO support
------------

The Linux runtimes do not link libgpiod directly. GPIO commands are enabled
only when the optional openhsp-gpio-gpiod package is installed. This keeps the
default openhsp package usable on systems without GPIO hardware or libgpiod,
while allowing Raspberry Pi and x86 single-board computer users to add GPIO
support separately.
